Spec: Agent-authorized multi-endpoint STUN discovery

Purpose:
  Derive real NAT observations using only the endpoints explicitly selected by the owning Agent.

Owns:
  ./linkgate_discovery.go
  ./linkgate_discovery_test.go

Must:
  Require a bounded canonical numeric IPv4 endpoint array in Agent mode; missing, malformed, duplicate or fake-IP configuration fails before network use.
  Reuse one UDP socket and count at least two distinct actual destinations before reporting sufficient observations, even when mappings are equal.
  Retain valid observations when another configured endpoint fails; never contact implicit public fallbacks or response-provided alternate addresses outside the configured list.
  Use upstream standard STUN source/transaction checks and bounded request timeouts, validating returned address and port before NAT classification.
  Emit only fixed aggregate status and counts; preserve stock discovery only outside Agent mode with no explicit configuration.
